IMPORT prelude

-- Victims of Crime Assistance Regulations 2007 (NT) -- THE TABLES: Schedule 1 (compensable violent acts and their
-- standard amounts), Schedule 2 (offences that may result in a category 1 or 2 psychological or psychiatric disorder)
-- and Schedule 3 (compensable injuries and standard amounts), with regs 4, 6, 7, 14 and 16(3) that read them.
-- Seat-neutral data; the rules that use it are in voca-core.l4, the questions in voca-seat.l4.
--
-- Edition: Regulations reprint REPV014R1, as in force at 25 March 2024, deposited at
-- subjects/au/nt/victims-of-crime-assistance-regulations-2007/registers/source-bundle/
-- Victims-of-Crime-Assistance-Regulations-2007-NT-current-reprint-REPV014R1.txt (an unofficial copy; see
-- SOURCE-LICENSE.md). Quoted under the NT licence ruling of 24 October 2026.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Victims of Crime Assistance Regulations 2007 -- the Schedules`

§§ `Regs 4, 6, 7 and 7A -- the offence, as the Schedules describe it`

-- One offence, in the terms the Schedules use. `section` is written as the Schedules write it: "208H", "127(1)(a)",
-- "130(3A)(b)", "192B", "211(1)". The date facts pick the Schedule headings that apply: "Criminal Code" (the Code as
-- now in force), "Criminal Code as in force before the commencement of Part 2 of the Criminal Justice Legislation
-- Amendment (Sexual Offences) Act 2023" (25 March 2024, Regulations endnote 2) and, in Schedule 2 only, "Criminal Code
-- as in force before the commencement of section 10 of the Criminal Code Amendment (Property Offences) Act 2023"
-- (read as the 2022 Act, No. 24 of 2022, commenced 30 April 2023: see NOTES.md finding 8).
DECLARE `Offence` HAS
    `section`                                                        IS A STRING
    `was an attempt`                                                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `was committed before 25 March 2024`                             IS A BOOLEAN
    `was committed before 30 April 2023`                             IS A BOOLEAN
    `the victim suffered serious harm as a direct result`            IS A BOOLEAN
    `was committed by the use or threatened use of an offensive weapon` IS A BOOLEAN
    `was committed by a person in the company of another person`     IS A BOOLEAN
    `the circumstance in old s 188(2)(a) applied`                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `the circumstance in old s 188(2)(c) applied`                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `the circumstance in old s 188(2)(k) applied`                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `the condition opposite it in Schedule 2 applied`                IS A BOOLEAN
    `how many related criminal acts the violent act is a series of`  IS A NUMBER
    `the related acts occurred over a period of time`                IS A BOOLEAN
    `the acts were committed against the same victim by the same offender` IS A BOOLEAN

-- reg 7: "A factor of aggravation applies for an offence if: (a) the victim suffers serious harm as a direct result of
-- the offence; or (b) the offence was committed by the use or threatened use of an offensive weapon; or (c) the
-- offence was committed by a person in the company of another person." Schedule 1, Part 4 counts them ("at least 2
-- factors of aggravation").
GIVEN `b` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`one if` `b` MEANS IF `b` THEN 1 ELSE 0

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN `Offence`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number of factors of aggravation for` `the offence` MEANS
        `one if` (`the offence`'s `the victim suffered serious harm as a direct result`)
    PLUS `one if` (`the offence`'s `was committed by the use or threatened use of an offensive weapon`)
    PLUS `one if` (`the offence`'s `was committed by a person in the company of another person`)

-- reg 6: "A violent act involves a pattern of abuse if: (a) the violent act is a series of 3 or more related criminal
-- acts that occur over a period of time; and (b) the acts are committed against the same victim by the same offender."
GIVEN `the offence` IS AN `Offence`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the violent act involves a pattern of abuse` `the offence` IF
        `the offence`'s `how many related criminal acts the violent act is a series of` AT LEAST 3
    AND `the offence`'s `the related acts occurred over a period of time`
    AND `the offence`'s `the acts were committed against the same victim by the same offender`

§§ `Schedule 1 -- categories of compensable violent acts (regs 4, 14)`

DECLARE `Schedule heading` IS ONE OF
    `Criminal Code`
    `Criminal Code before 25 March 2024`
    `Criminal Code before 30 April 2023`

-- The headings that apply to an offence. The current "Criminal Code" rows apply whenever the section exists; the older
-- headings only to an offence committed before the amendment they name.
GIVEN `the heading` IS A `Schedule heading`
      `the offence` IS AN `Offence`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the heading applies to` `the heading` `the offence` IF
    CONSIDER `the heading`
    WHEN `Criminal Code`                      THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Criminal Code before 25 March 2024` THEN `the offence`'s `was committed before 25 March 2024`
    WHEN `Criminal Code before 30 April 2023` THEN `the offence`'s `was committed before 30 April 2023`

-- The "Qualification" column of Schedule 1, Parts 1 to 3 and the first and last rows of Part 4.
DECLARE `Schedule 1 qualification` IS ONE OF
    `none`
    `if a factor of aggravation applies for the offence`
    `if the circumstances mentioned in section 188(2)(a), (c) and (k) of the Code applied`
    `if those section 188(2) circumstances applied and a factor of aggravation applies`

DECLARE `Schedule 1 row` HAS
    `part`          IS A NUMBER
    `heading`       IS A `Schedule heading`
    `attempt`       IS A BOOLEAN
    `sections`      IS A LIST OF STRING
    `qualification` IS A `Schedule 1 qualification`

GIVEN `p` IS A NUMBER
      `h` IS A `Schedule heading`
      `a` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s` IS A LIST OF STRING
      `q` IS A `Schedule 1 qualification`
GIVETH A `Schedule 1 row`
`s1` `p` `h` `a` `s` `q` MEANS
    `Schedule 1 row` WITH
        `part`          IS `p`
        `heading`       IS `h`
        `attempt`       IS `a`
        `sections`      IS `s`
        `qualification` IS `q`

-- Schedule 1, Parts 1 to 4, row by row ("An offence of attempting to commit an offence against section X" is a row
-- with attempt TRUE; reg 4(2) and reg 7A: a reference to an offence does not include an attempt, so a plain row does
-- not match an attempt). The two Part 4 rows that refer to other Parts ("An offence mentioned in Part 1, 2 or 3 ...
-- must involve a pattern of abuse"; "An offence mentioned in Part 3 -- If at least 2 factors of aggravation apply")
-- are rules, not rows: see `the Schedule 1 category of`.
`the Schedule 1 rows` MEANS
    LIST
        -- Part 1, Criminal Code
        `s1` 1 `Criminal Code` FALSE (LIST "208AB") `none`,
        `s1` 1 `Criminal Code` TRUE  (LIST "208H", "208HA") `none`,
        `s1` 1 `Criminal Code` FALSE (LIST "208HB", "208HC", "208HD") `none`,
        `s1` 1 `Criminal Code` TRUE  (LIST "208J", "208JA") `none`,
        `s1` 1 `Criminal Code` FALSE (LIST "208JB", "208JC", "208JD", "208JE", "208JF", "208JG", "208JH") `none`,
        `s1` 1 `Criminal Code` TRUE  (LIST "208K", "208KA") `none`,
        `s1` 1 `Criminal Code` FALSE (LIST "208KB", "208KC") `none`,
        `s1` 1 `Criminal Code` TRUE  (LIST "208LB", "208LC") `none`,
        `s1` 1 `Criminal Code` FALSE (LIST "208LD", "208LE") `none`,
        -- Part 1, Criminal Code as in force before 25 March 2024
        `s1` 1 `Criminal Code before 25 March 2024` TRUE  (LIST "127(1)(a)") `none`,
        `s1` 1 `Criminal Code before 25 March 2024` FALSE (LIST "127(1)(b)") `none`,
        `s1` 1 `Criminal Code before 25 March 2024` TRUE  (LIST "130(2)(a)", "130(3A)(a)") `none`,
        `s1` 1 `Criminal Code before 25 March 2024` FALSE (LIST "130(2)(b)", "130(3A)(b)") `none`,
        `s1` 1 `Criminal Code before 25 March 2024` FALSE (LIST "188") `if the circumstances mentioned in section 188(2)(a), (c) and (k) of the Code applied`,
        `s1` 1 `Criminal Code before 25 March 2024` TRUE  (LIST "192(3)", "192B") `none`,
        `s1` 1 `Criminal Code before 25 March 2024` FALSE (LIST "192(6)") `none`,
        -- Part 2, Criminal Code
        `s1` 2 `Criminal Code` FALSE (LIST "125D") `none`,
        `s1` 2 `Criminal Code` FALSE (LIST "208AB") `if a factor of aggravation applies for the offence`,
        `s1` 2 `Criminal Code` TRUE  (LIST "186B") `none`,
        `s1` 2 `Criminal Code` TRUE  (LIST "208H", "208HA") `if a factor of aggravation applies for the offence`,
        `s1` 2 `Criminal Code` FALSE (LIST "208H", "208HA") `none`,
        `s1` 2 `Criminal Code` FALSE (LIST "208HB", "208HC", "208HD") `if a factor of aggravation applies for the offence`,
        `s1` 2 `Criminal Code` TRUE  (LIST "208J", "208JA") `if a factor of aggravation applies for the offence`,
        `s1` 2 `Criminal Code` FALSE (LIST "208J", "208JA") `none`,
        `s1` 2 `Criminal Code` FALSE (LIST "208JB", "208JC", "208JD", "208JE", "208JF", "208JG", "208JH") `if a factor of aggravation applies for the offence`,
        `s1` 2 `Criminal Code` TRUE  (LIST "208K", "208KA") `if a factor of aggravation applies for the offence`,
        `s1` 2 `Criminal Code` FALSE (LIST "208K", "208KA") `none`,
        `s1` 2 `Criminal Code` FALSE (LIST "208KB", "208KC") `if a factor of aggravation applies for the offence`,
        `s1` 2 `Criminal Code` TRUE  (LIST "208LB", "208LC") `if a factor of aggravation applies for the offence`,
        `s1` 2 `Criminal Code` FALSE (LIST "208LB", "208LC") `none`,
        `s1` 2 `Criminal Code` FALSE (LIST "208LD", "208LE") `if a factor of aggravation applies for the offence`,
        -- Part 2, Criminal Code as in force before 25 March 2024
        `s1` 2 `Criminal Code before 25 March 2024` TRUE  (LIST "127(1)(a)") `if a factor of aggravation applies for the offence`,
        `s1` 2 `Criminal Code before 25 March 2024` FALSE (LIST "127(1)(a)") `none`,
        `s1` 2 `Criminal Code before 25 March 2024` FALSE (LIST "127(1)(b)") `if a factor of aggravation applies for the offence`,
        `s1` 2 `Criminal Code before 25 March 2024` TRUE  (LIST "130(2)(a)", "130(3A)(a)") `if a factor of aggravation applies for the offence`,
        `s1` 2 `Criminal Code before 25 March 2024` FALSE (LIST "130(2)(a)", "130(3A)(a)") `none`,
        `s1` 2 `Criminal Code before 25 March 2024` FALSE (LIST "130(2)(b)", "130(3A)(b)") `if a factor of aggravation applies for the offence`,
        `s1` 2 `Criminal Code before 25 March 2024` FALSE (LIST "188") `if those section 188(2) circumstances applied and a factor of aggravation applies`,
        `s1` 2 `Criminal Code before 25 March 2024` TRUE  (LIST "192(3)", "192B") `if a factor of aggravation applies for the offence`,
        `s1` 2 `Criminal Code before 25 March 2024` FALSE (LIST "192(3)") `none`,
        `s1` 2 `Criminal Code before 25 March 2024` FALSE (LIST "192(6)") `if a factor of aggravation applies for the offence`,
        `s1` 2 `Criminal Code before 25 March 2024` FALSE (LIST "192B") `none`,
        -- Part 3, Criminal Code
        `s1` 3 `Criminal Code` FALSE (LIST "125D") `if a factor of aggravation applies for the offence`,
        `s1` 3 `Criminal Code` FALSE (LIST "186B") `none`,
        `s1` 3 `Criminal Code` FALSE (LIST "208H", "208HA", "208J", "208JA", "208K", "208KA", "208LB", "208LC") `if a factor of aggravation applies for the offence`,
        -- Part 3, Criminal Code as in force before 25 March 2024
        `s1` 3 `Criminal Code before 25 March 2024` FALSE (LIST "127(1)(a)", "130(2)(a)", "130(3A)(a)") `if a factor of aggravation applies for the offence`,
        `s1` 3 `Criminal Code before 25 March 2024` FALSE (LIST "192(3)", "192B") `if a factor of aggravation applies for the offence`,
        -- Part 4, the two rows that name a section
        `s1` 4 `Criminal Code` FALSE (LIST "208JI") `none`,
        `s1` 4 `Criminal Code before 25 March 2024` FALSE (LIST "131A") `none`

GIVEN `the qualification` IS A `Schedule 1 qualification`
      `the offence`       IS AN `Offence`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Schedule 1 qualification is met` `the qualification` `the offence` IF
    CONSIDER `the qualification`
    WHEN `none` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `if a factor of aggravation applies for the offence` THEN
        `the number of factors of aggravation for` `the offence` AT LEAST 1
    WHEN `if the circumstances mentioned in section 188(2)(a), (c) and (k) of the Code applied` THEN
        `the old s 188 circumstances applied to` `the offence`
    WHEN `if those section 188(2) circumstances applied and a factor of aggravation applies` THEN
            `the old s 188 circumstances applied to` `the offence`
        AND `the number of factors of aggravation for` `the offence` AT LEAST 1
    WHERE
        GIVEN `o` IS AN `Offence`
        GIVETH A BOOLEAN
        DECIDE `the old s 188 circumstances applied to` `o` IF
                `o`'s `the circumstance in old s 188(2)(a) applied`
            AND `o`'s `the circumstance in old s 188(2)(c) applied`
            AND `o`'s `the circumstance in old s 188(2)(k) applied`

GIVEN `the row`     IS A `Schedule 1 row`
      `the offence` IS AN `Offence`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Schedule 1 row matches` `the row` `the offence` IF
        `the heading applies to` (`the row`'s `heading`) `the offence`
    AND `the row`'s `attempt` EQUALS `the offence`'s `was an attempt`
    AND elem (`the offence`'s `section`) (`the row`'s `sections`)
    AND `the Schedule 1 qualification is met` (`the row`'s `qualification`) `the offence`

-- The highest Part in which the offence appears in Parts 1 to 4 by name; 0 if none.
GIVEN `the offence` IS AN `Offence`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the highest Schedule 1 Part naming` `the offence` MEANS
    foldr (GIVEN `r`, `acc` YIELD IF `the Schedule 1 row matches` `r` `the offence` AND `r`'s `part` GREATER THAN `acc` THEN `r`'s `part` ELSE `acc`) 0 `the Schedule 1 rows`

-- Whether the offence appears in Part 3 by name.
GIVEN `the offence` IS AN `Offence`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the offence is mentioned in Part 3` `the offence` IF
    any (GIVEN `r` YIELD `r`'s `part` EQUALS 3 AND `the Schedule 1 row matches` `r` `the offence`) `the Schedule 1 rows`

-- regs 4(1), 14(1)-(3A): the category of a compensable violent act; 0 means the offence is not in Schedule 1, so the
-- violent act is not a compensable violent act (s 7(1) of the Act). Schedule 1, Part 4 also takes "An offence
-- mentioned in Part 1, 2 or 3, or a combination of those offences -- The offence or offences must involve a pattern of
-- abuse" and "An offence mentioned in Part 3 -- If at least 2 factors of aggravation apply for the offence".
-- READING: where an offence matches rows in more than one Part (an aggravated s 208AB is in Part 1 without a
-- qualification and in Part 2 "If a factor of aggravation applies"), the highest Part is its category. The
-- Regulations do not say (NOTES.md finding 6).
GIVEN `the offence` IS AN `Offence`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Schedule 1 category of` `the offence` MEANS
    IF     (`the named Part` AT LEAST 1 AND `the violent act involves a pattern of abuse` `the offence`)
        OR (`the offence is mentioned in Part 3` `the offence` AND `the number of factors of aggravation for` `the offence` AT LEAST 2)
    THEN 4
    ELSE `the named Part`
    WHERE
        `the named Part` MEANS `the highest Schedule 1 Part naming` `the offence`

-- Schedule 1, Part 5: "(a) for a category 1 compensable violent act -- an amount of $10 000; (b) ... category 2 --
-- $20 000; (c) ... category 3 -- $30 000; (d) ... category 4 -- $40 000." reg 14(4).
GIVEN `the category` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Schedule 1 standard amount for category` `the category` MEANS
    IF `the category` EQUALS 1 THEN 10000
    ELSE IF `the category` EQUALS 2 THEN 20000
         ELSE IF `the category` EQUALS 3 THEN 30000
              ELSE IF `the category` EQUALS 4 THEN 40000
                   ELSE 0

§§ `Schedule 2 -- offences that may result in a category 1 or 2 psychological or psychiatric disorder (reg 15)`

-- Schedule 2, row by row. A row with `needs the condition` TRUE has a qualification other than old s 188: s 196 "If
-- committed by a person on the person's unlawful entry of a building under (a) section 221 of the Code; or (b) section
-- 213 ... as in force immediately before the commencement of section 10 of the Criminal Code Amendment (Property
-- Offences) Act 2022"; s 218 "If committed in a circumstance mentioned in section 219(1) of the Code"; old s 211(1) "If
-- committed in a circumstance mentioned in section 211(2) of the Code". Old s 188: "If the circumstances mentioned in
-- section 188(2)(c) and (k) of the Code applied".
DECLARE `Schedule 2 row` HAS
    `heading`             IS A `Schedule heading`
    `sections`            IS A LIST OF STRING
    `needs the condition` IS A BOOLEAN
    `needs old s 188(2)(c) and (k)` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `h` IS A `Schedule heading`
      `s` IS A LIST OF STRING
      `c` IS A BOOLEAN
      `k` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Schedule 2 row`
`s2` `h` `s` `c` `k` MEANS
    `Schedule 2 row` WITH
        `heading`             IS `h`
        `sections`            IS `s`
        `needs the condition` IS `c`
        `needs old s 188(2)(c) and (k)` IS `k`

`the Schedule 2 rows` MEANS
    LIST
        `s2` `Criminal Code` (LIST "156", "160", "161A", "162", "165", "189", "194", "195") FALSE FALSE,
        `s2` `Criminal Code` (LIST "196") TRUE FALSE,
        `s2` `Criminal Code` (LIST "202") FALSE FALSE,
        `s2` `Criminal Code` (LIST "218") TRUE FALSE,
        `s2` `Criminal Code before 25 March 2024` (LIST "132(2)") FALSE FALSE,
        `s2` `Criminal Code before 25 March 2024` (LIST "188") FALSE TRUE,
        `s2` `Criminal Code before 25 March 2024` (LIST "192(7)") FALSE FALSE,
        `s2` `Criminal Code before 30 April 2023` (LIST "211(1)") TRUE FALSE

-- Schedule 2 offences are completed offences (reg 7A: no attempts).
GIVEN `the row`     IS A `Schedule 2 row`
      `the offence` IS AN `Offence`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Schedule 2 row matches` `the row` `the offence` IF
        `the heading applies to` (`the row`'s `heading`) `the offence`
    AND (NOT (`the offence`'s `was an attempt`))
    AND elem (`the offence`'s `section`) (`the row`'s `sections`)
    AND (    (NOT (`the row`'s `needs the condition`))
          OR `the offence`'s `the condition opposite it in Schedule 2 applied`)
    AND (    (NOT (`the row`'s `needs old s 188(2)(c) and (k)`))
          OR (    `the offence`'s `the circumstance in old s 188(2)(c) applied`
              AND `the offence`'s `the circumstance in old s 188(2)(k) applied`))

-- reg 15(1)(b), (2)(b)(i): "an offence against the Criminal Code specified in Schedule 1 or 2 to which the
-- qualification specified opposite applies".
GIVEN `the offence` IS AN `Offence`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the offence is specified in Schedule 1 or 2` `the offence` IF
        `the Schedule 1 category of` `the offence` AT LEAST 1
    OR  any (GIVEN `r` YIELD `the Schedule 2 row matches` `r` `the offence`) `the Schedule 2 rows`

§§ `Schedule 3 -- compensable injuries and standard amounts (reg 16)`

-- One leaf of the Schedule 3, Part 2 table. `item` is the table's numbering down to the leaf ("6.7(a)", "1.2(a)(ii)",
-- "9", "4"). `doubles` marks the items named in reg 16(3)(ab): "item 5.1, 5.2, 6.2 to 6.4, 6.7, 7.4(a), 8, 14.1 or
-- 14.4 that occurs on each side of the body -- double the amount specified opposite the injury".
DECLARE `Schedule 3 row` HAS
    `item`        IS A STRING
    `amount`      IS A NUMBER
    `doubles`     IS A BOOLEAN
    `description` IS A STRING

GIVEN `i` IS A STRING
      `a` IS A NUMBER
      `d` IS A BOOLEAN
      `t` IS A STRING
GIVETH A `Schedule 3 row`
`s3` `i` `a` `d` `t` MEANS
    `Schedule 3 row` WITH
        `item`        IS `i`
        `amount`      IS `a`
        `doubles`     IS `d`
        `description` IS `t`

-- Schedule 3, Part 2, every leaf, in the order of the table. Amounts in dollars, as printed.
`the Schedule 3 rows` MEANS
    LIST
        `s3` "1.1(a)"     3000  FALSE "Concussion lasting at least 1 week but not more than 13 weeks",
        `s3` "1.1(b)"     10000 FALSE "Persistent post concussive syndrome lasting more than 13 weeks",
        `s3` "1.2(a)(i)"  12000 FALSE "Structural brain injury with functional impairment lasting at least 1 week but not more than 26 weeks",
        `s3` "1.2(a)(ii)" 24000 FALSE "Structural brain injury with functional impairment lasting more than 26 weeks but not more than 52 weeks",
        `s3` "1.2(a)(iii)" 40000 FALSE "Structural brain injury with functional impairment lasting more than 52 weeks or permanently",
        `s3` "1.2(b)"     40000 FALSE "No effective control of functions lasting more than 52 weeks or permanently",
        `s3` "1.3"        15500 FALSE "Injury to vestibular system impairing balance for more than 52 weeks or permanently",
        `s3` "2(a)"       3000  FALSE "Superficial burns covering more than 4.5% TBSA, not affecting the face, genitals or anus",
        `s3` "2(b)"       7500  FALSE "Superficial burns to the face, genitals or anus covering more than 0.5% TBSA",
        `s3` "2(c)"       16000 FALSE "Partial/full thickness burns to the face, genitals, anus or hands covering more than 0.5% TBSA",
        `s3` "2(d)(i)"    3000  FALSE "Partial/full thickness burns covering more than 0.5% but not more than 4.5% TBSA",
        `s3` "2(d)(ii)"   8000  FALSE "Partial/full thickness burns covering more than 4.5% but not more than 18% TBSA",
        `s3` "2(d)(iii)"  20000 FALSE "Partial/full thickness burns covering more than 18% but not more than 27% TBSA",
        `s3` "2(d)(iv)"   40000 FALSE "Partial/full thickness burns covering more than 27% TBSA",
        `s3` "3(a)"       2000  FALSE "Disability from a disease or other recognised medical illness lasting more than 4 but not more than 13 weeks",
        `s3` "3(b)"       8000  FALSE "Disability from a disease or other recognised medical illness lasting more than 13 but not more than 26 weeks",
        `s3` "3(c)"       15500 FALSE "Disability from a disease or other recognised medical illness lasting more than 26 but not more than 52 weeks",
        `s3` "3(d)"       40000 FALSE "Disability from a disease or other recognised medical illness lasting more than 52 weeks or permanently",
        `s3` "4"          10000 FALSE "Domestic violence injuries",
        `s3` "5.1(a)"     8000  TRUE  "Loss of more than 50% of ear tissue but not whole ear",
        `s3` "5.1(b)"     20000 TRUE  "Loss of whole ear",
        `s3` "5.1(c)"     3500  TRUE  "Perforated ear drum",
        `s3` "5.1(d)(i)"  2500  TRUE  "Partial deafness of ear lasting more than 13 weeks but not more than 52 weeks",
        `s3` "5.1(d)(ii)" 7500  TRUE  "Partial deafness of ear lasting more than 52 weeks or permanently",
        `s3` "5.1(e)(i)"  6000  TRUE  "Total deafness of ear lasting more than 13 weeks but not more than 52 weeks",
        `s3` "5.1(e)(ii)" 20000 TRUE  "Total deafness of ear lasting more than 52 weeks or permanently",
        `s3` "5.1(f)(i)"  4000  TRUE  "Tinnitus lasting more than 13 weeks but not more than 52 weeks",
        `s3` "5.1(f)(ii)" 16000 TRUE  "Tinnitus lasting more than 52 weeks or permanently",
        `s3` "5.2(a)"     6000  TRUE  "Cataracts",
        `s3` "5.2(b)"     10000 TRUE  "Detached retina or dislocation of lens",
        `s3` "5.2(c)(i)"  3500  TRUE  "Double vision (diplopia) lasting more than 4 weeks but not more than 52 weeks",
        `s3` "5.2(c)(ii)" 24000 TRUE  "Double vision (diplopia) lasting more than 52 weeks or permanently",
        `s3` "5.2(d)"     5000  TRUE  "Glaucoma",
        `s3` "5.2(e)"     5000  TRUE  "Hyphaema",
        `s3` "5.2(f)"     40000 TRUE  "Loss of eye (enucleation)",
        `s3` "5.2(g)(i)"  2000  TRUE  "Permanent partial loss of vision of eye resulting in 6/9 vision",
        `s3` "5.2(g)(ii)" 4000  TRUE  "Permanent partial loss of vision of eye resulting in 6/12 vision",
        `s3` "5.2(g)(iii)" 12000 TRUE "Permanent partial loss of vision of eye resulting in 6/24 vision",
        `s3` "5.2(g)(iv)" 20000 TRUE  "Permanent partial loss of vision of eye resulting in 6/36 vision",
        `s3` "5.2(h)(i)"  30000 TRUE  "Complete loss of vision of eye (6/60 or greater) lasting more than 13 weeks but not permanently",
        `s3` "5.2(h)(ii)" 40000 TRUE  "Complete loss of vision of eye (6/60 or greater), permanently",
        `s3` "5.2(i)"     4000  TRUE  "Vitreous haemorrhage",
        `s3` "5.3(a)"     4000  FALSE "Facial numbness lasting more than 13 weeks",
        `s3` "5.3(b)"     8000  FALSE "Facial weakness significantly impacting facial expression or daily functioning",
        `s3` "5.3(c)"     4000  FALSE "Dislocation of jaw (temporomandibular joint)",
        `s3` "5.3(d)"     7500  FALSE "Dysfunction of temporomandibular joint lasting more than 52 weeks or permanently",
        `s3` "5.4(a)"     3000  FALSE "Deviated nasal septum",
